{"additions":535,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nvig polls GitHub through `gh` (runs watch, PR checks watch, running-job log polls). A busy session could exhaust the 5,000 req/h quota, and rate-limit errors were shown as plain fetch failures while polling kept hammering the API. This PR detects rate-limit rejections centrally, backs off all GitHub-page polling exponentially, surfaces the state in the status bar, and makes the poll interval configurable.\n\nCloses #135\n\n## Changes\n\n**Rate-limit detection** (`src/github/domain/client.rs`)\n- `is_rate_limited(&str)` recognises the `gh` error signatures: REST `API rate limit exceeded` (and `secondary rate limit`), GraphQL `rate limit already exceeded` / `RATE_LIMITED`. Existing `Result<_, String>` signatures are unchanged; classification happens where the error strings are drained.\n- `fetch_rate_limit_reset()` reads the quota reset time via `gh api rate_limit --jq .resources.core.reset` — that endpoint is not rate-limited. It is called **once per backoff episode**; the status bar recomputes the remaining minutes from the stored timestamp.\n\n**Backoff** (`src/github/state.rs`)\n- A rate-limited fetch result engages a page-wide `RateLimitBackoff` (30s → 60s → … capped at 10min, pure `next_backoff` function) instead of the red error line. While the window is open, `on_tick` returns early, suspending the runs watch, the checks watch and the jobs/log polls.\n- After the window, polling resumes; a rejected retry doubles the delay (rejections inside the same window — e.g. issue+PR+run lists failing together — don't escalate). Any successful fetch clears the backoff. Manual `r` bypasses the gate entirely (`refresh` / `refresh_detail` don't tick).\n- Status bar shows `⚠ GitHub rate limited (resets in Nm)` (or `resets soon` once the reset time passed) in yellow while the backoff is active.\n\n**Configurable interval** (`src/core/config/loader.rs`, `merge.rs`, `assets/default.kdl`)\n- New top-level `github-poll-interval \"5s\"` (default 5s, floor 2s, reuses `parse_interval`), replace-wholesale merge semantics, validated in `Config::with_user`. It drives the runs watch, the PR checks watch (previously hardcoded 10s → now the configured interval) and the running-job log poll, threaded via `GhDetailViewPane::set_poll_interval`.\n- Documented in `docs/config.md` (merge table, schema, own section) and the READMEs.\n\n## Audit findings (inactive-page polling)\n\n- `App::on_tick` dispatches only to `self.pages[active_page]`, so no GitHub (or Projects) polling runs while the page is inactive. All `gh` invocations are one-shot worker threads spawned per fetch — there are no long-lived `spawn`ed loops or timers that could outlive a page switch.\n- The Projects page has no `on_tick` at all; board loads happen only on activation/selection, showing the disk cache first and warming an in-memory board cache.\n- GitHub list panes (`gh_list.rs::initialize`) load the disk cache first and then do a single background refresh, and only on the first activation of the page (guarded by `initialized`) — nothing refetches at process startup.\n- `src/docker` / `src/procs` poll local commands only (out of scope); the Procs sampler already pauses on inactive pages.\n- One deliberate behaviour: if nothing is actively polling (no active runs, no watch mode, no running log), a backoff that was engaged stays displayed until a manual `r` succeeds — the warning is recomputed from the stored reset time, so it degrades to `resets soon` and never re-polls `rate_limit`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `client.rs`: rate-limit signature fixtures (REST, secondary, GraphQL, negatives).\n- `state.rs::rate_limit`: backoff progression (30→60→…→600 cap), reset-time formatting (`resets in 12m` / `resets soon`, minutes round up), drain-level behaviour (backoff engages without touching the error line, same-burst rejections don't escalate, a post-window rejection doubles, success clears), and `on_tick` suspension of the runs watch.\n- `loader.rs`: `github-poll-interval` default / override / floor validation; `merge.rs`: replace-wholesale.\n- `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets` (zero warnings), `cargo test` (316 passed).\n\n## Not verified\n\n- No live rate-limit exhaustion was reproduced against the real GitHub API; detection is tested against the documented `gh` error strings, and the `gh api rate_limit` probe path was not exercised end-to-end.\n- No demo tape: the behaviour is an error path (and the config knob changes no visible UI), so per the issue no GIF was recorded or re-recorded.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":12,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T06:22:48Z","deletions":31,"headRefName":"feat/rate-limit-backoff","labels":[],"number":137,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdFavw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere is a confirmed behavioral inconsistency in how rate-limit backoff is cleared on success, and the repo’s tape/GIF update convention is not met for the new user-visible GitHub UI behavior.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR improves the GitHub page’s polling behavior by detecting `gh` rate-limit errors, applying an exponential backoff across GitHub-page polling, surfacing a status-bar warning, and adding a configurable polling interval via config.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add centralized rate-limit detection and a one-shot quota reset probe via `gh api rate_limit`.\n- Introduce a page-wide exponential backoff that suspends automatic GitHub polling and displays a status-bar notice while active.\n- Add `github-poll-interval` config (default 5s, min 2s) and thread it through runs refresh, PR checks watch, and jobs/log polling.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `src/github/state.rs` | Implements rate-limit backoff state, suspension of polling on tick, and status-bar notice text. |\r\n| `src/github/panes/detail_view/mod.rs` | Adds a configurable poll interval for checks watch and run detail polling. |\r\n| `src/github/panes/detail_view/log.rs` | Makes running-job log polling interval configurable. |\r\n| `src/github/panes/detail_view/jobs.rs` | Makes jobs polling interval configurable and updates tests accordingly. |\r\n| `src/github/domain/client.rs` | Adds `gh` rate-limit error classification and reset-time fetch helper, plus unit tests. |\r\n| `src/core/ui/status_bar.rs` | Renders the GitHub rate-limit warning in the status bar. |\r\n| `src/core/config/merge.rs` | Adds replace-wholesale merge semantics for `github-poll-interval` with a test. |\r\n| `src/core/config/loader.rs` | Adds `github-poll-interval` parsing/validation and tests (default/override/floor). |\r\n| `README.md` | Documents the new configurable polling interval and rate-limit backoff behavior. |\r\n| `docs/README.ja.md` | Documents the same behavior in Japanese. |\r\n| `docs/config.md` | Documents the new config key, schema, merge behavior, and rate-limit backoff behavior. |\r\n| `assets/default.kdl` | Adds the default `github-poll-interval \"5s\"` setting with comments. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 12/12 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:26:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"9a70900999879b550ea1a29fa590bd84d8aac2eb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdJgQA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe current drain logic can suppress engaging the rate-limit backoff when a rate-limited error and a successful fetch arrive in the same batch, potentially causing silent partial failures without warning/backoff.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**README.md:219**\n* This paragraph still says the runs list refreshes every 5 seconds, but the interval is now configurable via `github-poll-interval`. The docs should reflect that the default is 5s and the actual value may differ.\n```\nThe third column lists the latest 50 workflow runs (`gh run list`) with their\nstatus, workflow, run number, branch, event, duration (elapsed while running)\nand age; while any run is queued or in progress the list refreshes every 5\nseconds (`github-poll-interval` in the config). Selecting a run fills the detail area with its jobs and their steps\nnested underneath (failed steps in red) in the **Jobs** sub-pane; `Enter` on a\n```\n**docs/README.ja.md:217**\n* ここは「5 秒ごと」と固定のように読めますが、ポーリング間隔は `github-poll-interval` で設定可能になっています。既定値が 5 秒であることと、実際の更新間隔は設定値に従うことが分かる表現にしたいです。\n```\n3 列目には最新 50 件のワークフロー実行（`gh run list`）がステータス・ワークフロー名・実行番号・\nブランチ・イベント・所要時間（実行中は経過時間）・経過日時とともに並び、queued / in progress の\n実行がある間は 5 秒ごと（設定の `github-poll-interval`）に更新されます。実行を選ぶと詳細エリアの **Jobs** サブペインにジョブが\nステップをぶら下げたツリーで表示され（失敗したステップは赤）、ジョブまたはステップで `Enter` を\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 12/12 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:38:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"89d03584d7aedc23b38761412a9158ba633811a9"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdNMxA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:48:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"89d03584d7aedc23b38761412a9158ba633811a9"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdNNPQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T06:48:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"89d03584d7aedc23b38761412a9158ba633811a9"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:51:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33365856823/job/99406248915","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:51:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:37:21Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852716/job/99403277949","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:37Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852748/job/99403278220","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:37:02Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852716/job/99403277829","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:38:04Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852716/job/99403278024","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:38:04Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852716/job/99403677806","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:38:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:51:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33365856823/job/99406249489","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:51:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:58Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852748/job/99403278196","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:37:40Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33364852748/job/99403278043","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:36:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T06:51:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33365856823/job/99406275135","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-31T06:51:14Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ GitHub polling: rate-limit detection, backoff and a configurable interval"}
